    "body": "## Summary\n\nADR-039 Commit 2: `box-sizing: border-box`. **Risk-isolated** — changes how `width`, `height`, and their min/max clamps are interpreted.\n\n## The semantics shift\n\n| Value | `width: 100px; padding: 10px; border-width: 5px` |\n|---|---|\n| `content-box` (default) | Total border-box = **130px** (100 + 20 + 10) |\n| `border-box` | Total border-box = **100px** (content = 70px) |\n\nApplied uniformly to `width`, `height`, `min-width`, `max-width`, `min-height`, `max-height`.\n\n## What ships\n\n`layout_element` gains `bool border_box` computed once after `ComputedStyle` resolves. All six width/height/clamp blocks add a border-box branch that subtracts padding + border from the value before treating it as content dimension.\n\n## Measured delta (viewport 1774)\n\n7 first-viewport elements have `box-sizing: border-box` in Wikipedia CSS. After this commit:\n- Their border-box widths are unchanged (spec-correct)\n- Their content areas shrink by padding + border\n- Elements that previously overflowed by padding + border now fit\n\n**The specific first-viewport delta is measured in the render comparison in the commit message.** If box-sizing causes visible regressions, this commit is isolated for easy revert.\n\n## Honest finding: `border` shorthand limitation\n\nInitial tests used `border: 5px solid black` which ADR-012 does NOT expand. Only `border-width` longhand is expanded. Test setup was wrong; implementation was correct. Fixed to use `border-width: 5px`.\n\n**Real-world impact**: Wikipedia uses `border: 1px solid X` shorthand in many places. Those borders are currently **invisible** — the shorthand isn't expanded. **Pre-existing**, not introduced by ADR-039. Deferred to a small future ADR (\"border shorthand expansion\", ~20 lines).\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 494 / 1881\n- After: **500 / 1894** (+6 / +13)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\nNew tests in `test_box_model.cpp` (6):\n- border-box width includes padding+border (total = 100)\n- content-box width excludes padding (total = 130)\n- border-box height includes padding+border\n- border-box + width 100% fits parent exactly (no overflow)\n- border-box + tiny width + big padding clamps content to 0\n- border-box + max-width interpreted at border-box dimension\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| All 6 box-sizing tests pass | ✅ |\n| Full suite 500 / 1894 | ✅ |\n| No regressions in prior tests | ✅ |\n| First-viewport PNG diff | measured in commit |\n| Icon still w=20 h=20 | ✅ |\n\n## Revert path\n\nIf box-sizing causes visible regressions, `git revert` this commit alone leaves Commit 1 (height + min/max + overflow) intact. Two-commit shipping was designed for this.\n\n## What's next\n\n1. **Post-merge**: open the render PNG at `/tmp/wiki-adr039-c2.png` — verify article body looks correct with border-box applied\n2. **Docs close** ADR-039 (with two honest findings: 185px gap misdiagnosis from Commit 1 + border shorthand limitation from Commit 2)\n3. **ADR-040**: `parent_content_height` threading (unblocks % heights), `overflow: auto/scroll`, `aspect-ratio`, `border` shorthand expansion\n\nRefs #198\n",
